t\\\" for check faults (no code). Agent faults (code ERR_*) excluded.\\n\\nThreshold: tally distinct models per fault key (scenario, fault_class, tool) across trial rows; ≥ min(3, configured.len()) distinct models → proposal. Wait — brief says \\\"tool fault observed in trial rows from 3 distinct models\\\" for the same fault key. Use configured_models for threshold like report.rs: min(3, configured_models.len()), error if empty.\\n\\nThe `scenario_tool_of` callback: maps scenario name → recorded tool from scenario definition (Option<&str>). Proposals key repo on that recorded tool; row tool kept as provenance. If scenario_tool_of returns None? Loud error? The brief says proposals keyed on scenario recorded tool; if unknown scenario → loud error (report.rs convention: refuse loudly). But for synthetic rows in tests we supply the mapping.\\n\\nNow, the row model: trial rows may lack model (tier-1) — those don't count toward distinct models but occurrences counted? For routing proposals, only tier-2 (with model) rows contribute models. Occurrences: count check failures regardless.\\n\\nDesign of src/routing.rs:\\n\\n```rust\\n//! Purpose: dry-run fault routing — proposals for tool-fault tickets in the tool's repo.\\n//! Responsibilities: filter tier-2 report rows' failing checks to tool faults (no `code`), tally distinct models per fault key, apply the min(3,|registry|) routing threshold, and emit proposal rows with the fingerprint token and full machine-checkable schema.\\n//! Rationale: openspec add-fault-ticket-routing — the fault taxonomy routes tool faults to tickets; dry-run default keeps cross-repo writes behind an explicit opt-in (evallerina-2bz), and the schema makes the CI artifact reviewable without reading code.\\n```\\n\\nStruct ProposalRow (serialize to JSON):\\n- tool (recorded tool — repo keying), repo: Option<String> (None until mapped? For dry-run, unmapped → skipped with reason unmapped_tool; repo null), scenario, fault_class, token, decision, reason, bd_issue_id (null), row_provenance {scenario, model, tool} — but row_provenance per row... proposals are per fault key, yet row_provenance has model. Hmm: spec says each proposal row carries row_provenance (report row scenario/model/tool values). Since a proposal aggregates multiple rows, row_provenance could be the aggregated distinct models? Design.md schema example: row_provenance: {\\\"scenario\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"tool\\\": \\\"...\\\"}. With multiple models, maybe row_provenance carries distinct models list? The spec text says \\\"report row scenario/model/tool values\\\". I'll make row_provenance an array of provenance per contributing row: {\\\"scenario\\\", \\\"model\\\", \\\"tool\\\"} entries. Design example shows single object but arrays are compatible enough; tests are mine. Keep it as array of objects (models distinct). Actually simpler: row_provenance: {\\\"models\\\": [...distinct...], \\\"rows\\\": n}? Stick to spec fields: scenario, model, tool. I'll emit one provenance entry per contributing tier-2 row (deduped by model): array of {scenario, model, tool}.\\n\\nSince one proposal per fault key, and fault key includes scenario, provenance scenario is same; models vary. I'll produce rows: Vec<serde_json::Value> directly? Better typed struct then serialize. Keep ProposalRow struct with serde. But row_provenance array of structs — fine.\\n\\nDecision logic in dry-run: above-threshold → \\\"dry_run\\\" (phase 1 always dry-run; \\\"filed\\\"/\\\"existing\\\" come in phase 2). Unmapped tool (scenario_tool_of gives tool not in routing.toml map, or no mapping) → \\\"skipped\\\" reason \\\"unmapped_tool\\\". Above threshold but tool unmapped → still propose with skipped? Spec: \\\"unmapped tool is skipped, not fatal\\\" — decision skipped. I'll emit proposal rows only for above-threshold faults; decision dry_run if mapped, skipped/unmapped_tool if not mapped.\\n\\nAPI:\\n\\n```rust\\npub fn propose(\\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\\n    configured_models: &[String],\\n    scenario_tool_of: &dyn Fn(&str) -> Option<&str>,\\n    repo_map: &BTreeMap<String, String>,   // tool -> repo path (from routing.toml)\\n) -> Result<Vec<serde_json::Value>, String>\\n```\\n\\nErrors: empty registry → loud (mirror report.rs). Row parsing errors loud: missing fields etc. Unknown scenario (no recorded tool) → loud error? Brief 1.5: \\\"proposals key the repo on the scenario definition's recorded tool\\\" — the callback supplies it. If callback returns None → loud error \\\"scenario has no recorded tool — refusing to route\\\" (never silent bucket). That matches report.rs convention for unknown scenarios.\\n\\nTOML parsing: does the crate have `toml` dependency? Check Cargo.toml. If not, add `toml` to deps. routing.toml parse function `parse_routing_toml(&str) -> Result<BTreeMap<String,String>, String>` and `resolve_repo(path) -> PathBuf` (absolute → as-is; relative → git root join). Running `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` in tests: the test env is inside a git repo (evallerina) — fine, but to keep tests hermetic, resolve_repo takes a `repo_root: &Path` parameter and a separate helper discovers git root (not unit-tested, or test via std::process in integration test — that's fine since tests run in repo). I'll make `resolve_repo(repo: &str, root: &Path) -> Result<String, String>` pure, and a `discover_root()` that shells out. Tests use temp dirs as root.\\n\\nCheck Cargo.toml for toml dep.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-4b6319e7-6984-4a54-904e-a634bea54641","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"Cargo.toml","offset":1,"limit":40}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1100,"output":1550,"cacheRead":65920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1527,"totalTokens":68570,"cost":{"input":0.000165,"output":0.000775,"cacheRead":0.0019776,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0029176}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792426212466,"responseId