loud error? Brief 1.5: \\\"proposals key the repo on the scenario definition's recorded tool\\\" — the callback supplies it. If callback returns None → loud error \\\"scenario has no recorded tool — refusing to route\\\" (never silent bucket). That matches report.rs convention for unknown scenarios.\\n\\nTOML parsing: does the crate have `toml` dependency? Check Cargo.toml. If not, add `toml` to deps. routing.toml parse function `parse_routing_toml(&str) -> Result<BTreeMap<String,String>, String>` and `resolve_repo(path) -> PathBuf` (absolute → as-is; relative → git root join). Running `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` in tests: the test env is inside a git repo (evallerina) — fine, but to keep tests hermetic, resolve_repo takes a `repo_root: &Path` parameter and a separate helper discovers git root (not unit-tested, or test via std::process in integration test — that's fine since tests run in repo). I'll make `resolve_repo(repo: &str, root: &Path) -> Result<String, String>` pure, and a `discover_root()` that shells out. Tests use temp dirs as root.\\n\\nCheck Cargo.toml for toml dep.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-4b6319e7-6984-4a54-904e-a634bea54641","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"Cargo.toml","offset":1,"limit":40}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1100,"output":1550,"cacheRead":65920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1527,"totalTokens":68570,"cost":{"input":0.000165,"output":0.000775,"cacheRead":0.0019776,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0029176}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792426212466,"responseId":"gen-1792426212-jXQaWXBmFDT9JaFtCjE2","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-4b6319e7-6984-4a54-904e-a634bea54641","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[package]\nname = \"evallerina\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\ndescription = \"Eval battery for the dulce-de-leche tool family: do LLM agents actually use the su